== ws client macos wizard
At a terminal the stages open as two lists, by the machine each runs on, and the ones chosen run. The stages run under a lock, and what stays by hand is listed after a run in which a stage acted. Under --check each stage prints what it would do and changes nothing.

Usage:
  ws client macos wizard [flags]

Flags:
      --check    print what each stage would do and change nothing
  -h, --help     help for wizard
      --update   install the latest ws first, and run it in place of this one

Global Flags:
      --plain           print lines, with no full-screen display
      --server string   the server to act on, which may be left out where there is one
